              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "casabo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very tasty and pretty easy to make as well. I loved the blend of spices. As a carnivore, I decided to add chicken. With the chicken, it probably does not need as much edamame as the original recipe calls for (there was a lot of edamame!) Yum!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tara Renner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great light dinner! I didn't have broccoli so I lightly steamed a cut up cauliflower instead, and subbed that. I doubled up the spices, kept everything else the same. At the end I sprinkled the top with chopped cilantro and lemon juice - really took it over the top. I wasn't sure if the yogurt would add much, but wow it sure did. I served each plate with a plop of yogurt on top of the couscous and it was wonderful. Will make again!",
            "datePublished": "2022-04-09T00:43:14.458Z"
          },
